TITLE:: RERoutine
summary:: A Routine the score recorder can see
categories:: Libraries>reCording
related:: Guides/reCording, Classes/RETap, Classes/REScoreRecorder

DESCRIPTION::
A Routine made with code::RETap.routine { }:: (or this class) carries the cause open when it was created (the code line or the input being recorded, link::Classes/RETap#*frame::) and the object whose work it does (code::by::). What it does to the reCurrent objects is the program's work, level 2: recorded under that cause when link::Classes/REScoreRecorder#-level2:: is on, and a replay that defers the cause plays it from the take instead of running the Routine (the reCording guide, "Levels"). A plain Routine's actions are seen by no one. With nothing armed it is a Routine like any other.

code::RETask:: is a Task whose Routine is tagged (code::RETap.task::); code::REEventStreamPlayer:: an EventStreamPlayer whose playing Routine is tagged (link::Classes/RCBeat:: plays its pattern through one, the beat as doer).

CLASSMETHODS::

METHOD:: new
argument:: func
argument:: stackSize
argument:: by
argument:: cause
The frame (nil: the one open now). Made inside a tagged Routine, a new one inherits its cause and doer: a seeded draw (link::Classes/RCUtil#*seeded::), a worker a loop spawns.

INSTANCEMETHODS::

METHOD:: cause
METHOD:: by

EXAMPLES::

code::
RETap.routine { 8.do { |i| ~b.set(\amp, i / 8); 1.wait } }.play(~song.clock);
RETap.task({ loop { ~batch.editAttr("gain", 1.0.rand); 4.wait } }, ~song.clock, by: ~batch).play;
::
